  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ara Tiendas Green Loan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ara Tiendas (Ara), a chain of neighborhood retail stores in Colombia, has requested IFC to provide a long-term loan to partially finance the construction of two distribution centers which will be EDGE-Advanced certified (the Project) to provide logistic support to its stores.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFC expects the Project to increase customer access to affordable and high-quality retail services, meeting the increasing demand for more affordable retail services in Colombia, environmental effects, as well as significant economy-wide effects through the creation of direct jobs and increased demand for goods and services from local businesses. At the market level, IFC expects the Project to contribute to improving the competitiveness of the grocery retail market, especially the discount segment, in Colombia through demonstration channels.</narrative>
  </description>
